Gui was away on holiday on August 26 when a glacier collapsed in Nepal, triggering a massive mudflow and floods that travelled 22km (14 miles) in just seven minutes, flattening the entire Gyirong Port area. Many of his colleagues were lost in the disaster.

Returning to the site, Gui found the 20-metre (65 feet) port building that had survived previous heavy floods as well as strong earthquakes completely gone.

